after building: groups=1 haptic bonds=1
  group 0: atoms [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]
  bond 0: type=haptic begin=group 0 [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] end=atom 5 (Fe)
group countAtoms=5

*** the graph is untouched (isolation invariant of #3837) ***
bond count unchanged: True
implicit hydrogens unchanged: True
valences unchanged: True
bonds of the molecule: 5

*** what the API builds survives a KET round-trip ***
reloaded: groups=1 haptic bonds=1
  group 0: atoms [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]
  bond 0: type=haptic begin=group 0 [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] end=atom 5 (Fe)

*** what KET brings in is visible through the API ***
from KET: groups=1 haptic bonds=1
  group 0: atoms [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
  bond 0: type=haptic begin=atom 0 (Fe) end=group 0 [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
getAttachmentGroup(0) countAtoms=5
getHapticBond(0) type=haptic

*** clone keeps them, a submolecule applies the all-or-nothing rule ***
clone: groups=1 haptic bonds=1
  group 0: atoms [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]
  bond 0: type=haptic begin=group 0 [0, 1, 2, 3, 4] end=atom 5 (Fe)
whole ring without the metal: groups=1 haptic bonds=0
  group 0: atoms [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]
part of the ring: groups=0 haptic bonds=0

*** formats that cannot express a haptic bond omit it, without failing ***
smiles             saved
canonical smiles   saved
cml                saved

*** V3000 writes the bond out, V2000 omits it (#3840) ***
V3000 carries ENDPTS: True
the group gets a star atom back: True
V2000 carries ENDPTS: False

*** V3000 absorbs the star of a haptic record, not a variable one's ***
haptic star in the structure: False
haptic group anchor: none
variable attachment anchor: atom 7 (*)
KET anchor: none

*** membership can be replaced ***
after setAttachmentGroupAtoms: atoms [0, 1, 2]

*** errors ***
group to group           molecule: a haptic bond between two attachment groups is not allowed
bond to own member       molecule: atom 0 is a member of the attachment group it would be bonded to
partner joins group      molecule: atom 5 is bonded to the attachment group it would join
atom out of range        core: indigoAddAttachmentGroup(): atom index 99 out of range
no such group            core: indigoGetAttachmentGroup(): no attachment group with index 99
no such haptic bond      core: indigoGetHapticBond(): no haptic bond with index 99
empty group              core: indigoAddAttachmentGroup(): no atoms were given

*** removing a group takes its bonds with it ***
groups=1 haptic bonds=0
removed group is gone    core: attachment group 0 does not exist any more

*** removing a haptic bond leaves the group alone ***
groups=1 haptic bonds=0

*** a group has a charge and a radical of its own ***
zeise-salt-hydrate.ket:SUCCEED
as loaded: charge=0 radical=0
after setting: charge=-1 radical=102
atom charges unchanged: True
the same group as the end of its bond: charge=-1 radical=102
zeise-salt-hydrate-charged.ket:SUCCEED
zeise-salt-hydrate-charged.mol:SUCCEED
read back from KET: charge=-1 radical=102
read back from V3000: charge=-1 radical=102
unknown radical          core: Unknown radical type
same on an atom          core: Unknown radical type

*** every radical value, and back to none ***
singlet: set 101, read 101
doublet: set 102, read 102
triplet: set 103, read 103
none: set 0, read 0
charge set back: 0
zeise-salt-hydrate.ket:SUCCEED

*** two groups keep their own values ***
group 0: charge=1 radical=0
group 1: charge=2 radical=103
removed: charge          core: attachment group 0 does not exist any more
removed: setCharge       core: attachment group 0 does not exist any more
removed: radical         core: attachment group 0 does not exist any more
removed: setRadical      core: attachment group 0 does not exist any more
the other group is as it was: charge=2 radical=103

*** a view taken from the molecule follows the group ***
before: charge=0 radical=0
after setCharge: charge=-1 radical=0
after setRadical: charge=-1 radical=102

*** a group of a query molecule takes them as well ***
charge=-1 radical=103

*** no other atom call takes a group, and no other object these ***
resetCharge              core: <attachment group> does not represent an atom
resetRadical             core: <attachment group> does not represent an atom
radicalElectrons         core: <attachment group> does not represent an atom
charge of a bond         core: <bond> does not represent an atom
of a haptic bond         core: <haptic bond> does not represent an atom

*** V3000 keeps the charge of a haptic group only ***
variable attachment      molfile saver: attachment group 0 has charge -1 and radical 0, which V3000 can keep only on the star of a haptic bond record
variable-attachment-charged.ket:SUCCEED
